  "title": "Ph Life Insurance Handbook — 4. Beneficiaries Designation and Rules",
  "content": "## 4. Beneficiaries Designation and Rules\n- **Primary vs Contingent Beneficiaries**:\n  - Primary Beneficiaries: Receive proceeds upon the insured's demise.\n  - Contingent Beneficiaries: Receive proceeds if all primary beneficiaries predecease the insured.\n- **Revocable vs Irrevocable**:\n  - Revocable: The policyholder can change beneficiaries at any time without their consent.\n  - Irrevocable: The beneficiary's written consent is required for policy amendments, withdrawals, or beneficiary changes.\n- **Eligible Beneficiaries**: Under Philippine law, beneficiaries must have an insurable interest (spouse, legitimate or illegitimate children, parents, siblings, or legal dependents).\n\n---",
